TypeScript: Introduction :

TypeScript (TS) ek open-source, strongly-typed, object-oriented, compiled language hai
jo JavaScript ka superset hai.

TypeScript ka main goal hai:

✔ JavaScript ko safer banana
✔ Errors ko runtime se hataakar compile time par pakadna
✔ Large projects ko maintainable & scalable banana
✔ Developer experience improve karna (Auto-complete, IntelliSense, refactoring)

🔵 2. TypeScript Kyun Banaya Gaya?

JavaScript dynamic language hai:

Variables ka type change ho sakta hai

Objects me wrong properties daal sakte ho

Functions galat input accept kar lete hain

Errors runtime me milte hain (user ke saamne)

TypeScript inh problems ko solve karta hai:

Compile time par error detection

Strict type checking

Developer ko intelligent suggestions

Large team me code consistency

Large codebases me maintainability

🔵 3. TypeScript Ka Kaam Karne Ka Process (Architecture)
Step 1: You write .ts file
Step 2: TypeScript Compiler (tsc) type-checking karta hai
Step 3: Clean, error-free JavaScript generate hota hai
Step 4: Browser/Node.js JS ko run karta hai

🔵 4. TypeScript Key Features

1️⃣ Static Typing (Strong Typing)
Variables, functions, objects — sabke types define hote hain.

let age: number = 22;

2️⃣ Type Inference
Agar type nahi likho, TS khud detect karleta hai.

let name = "Ashutosh"; // inferred as string

3️⃣ Better IntelliSense

TypeScript IDE ko semantic information deta hai, jisse:
autocomplete
suggestions
refactoring
navigation
documentation
sab smart ban jaate hain.

interface User {
name: string;
age: number;
}

4️⃣ Interfaces

Objects ke structure define karna.

interface User {
name: string;
age: number;
}

5️⃣ Generics

Reusable aur type-safe components/functions.

function identity<T>(value: T): T {
return value;
}

6️⃣ Enums

Constants ko group karne ka elegant tarika.

7️⃣ Access Modifiers

OOP ke real power:

public

private

protected

readonly

8️⃣ Type Aliases

Custom types banane ka simple tarika.

🔵 5. TypeScript Important Concepts (Industry-Level)
✔ Union Types
let value: string | number;

✔ Intersection Types

Objects combine karna.

✔ Literal Types

Fixed values allow karna.

✔ Utility Types (VERY IMPORTANT)
Partial
Required
Pick
Omit
Readonly
Record
ReturnType

Industry me bahut use hote hain.
✔ Narrowing
TS ko batana ki variable kis type ka ho sakta hai.

🔵 6. TypeScript vs JavaScript
| Feature | JavaScript | TypeScript |
| ----------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------- |
| Typing | Dynamic | Static |
| Error Detection | Runtime | Compile time |
| Maintainability | Hard in large projects | Easy in large projects |
| IDE Support | Average | Best in class |
| Learning Curve | Easy | Slightly higher |
| Execution | Direct | Compiled to JS |
| Industry Standard | Good | Excellent |

